<title>GREECE: ATHLETICS-ZELEZNY OUT OF JAVELIN FINAL.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-ZELEZNY OUT OF JAVELIN FINAL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>World and Olympic champion Jan Zelezny of the Czech Republic was eliminated from the world men's javelin final on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The world record holder failed to record a mark at his first two tries and recorded 82.06 metres with his third attempt.</p>
<p>He ended in ninth place and missed the cut for the final eight who take the last three throws.</p>
</text>
